    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0747" n="1481" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1481"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to the Minister for Foreign Affairs of
                        Venezuela.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April 15,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your excellency’s letter of the 29th ultimo, with which was inclosed an
                    exemplified copy of a resolution of the Venezuelan Congress, under the same
                    date, expressing appreciation of a resolution of the Congress of the United
                    States, approved February 20, last, whereby that body earnestly recommended to
                    the favorable consideration of both the parties in interest the reference to
                    arbitration of the boundary dispute between Great Britain and Venezuela.</p>
                <p>I shall be pleased to bring your letter and its inclosure to the knowledge of the
                    President.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
